{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Planning receipt — next four comment-remediation children\n\nImmutable audit basis: `d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84` (also the clean code-worktree HEAD and `origin/main` during preparation).\n\nSelection/ranking:\n- Rechecked the 14 eligible open, unassigned direct children and ranked them by declared file-impact breadth, preserving the audited order for ties.\n- Selected the first four: `talkable-marmatite-agouti` (10 files), `doddered-undercover-alligator` (11), `fishy-dinky-urus` (11), and `dripping-captious-arctichare` (17). Every remaining ranked candidate had 18 files.\n- Live MCP preflight immediately before editing confirmed all four were still open, unassigned, unsigned, had no retained plan-review result, and remained direct children of `hopeful-deserved-needletail`.\n\nAudited prose inventory:\n- `talkable-marmatite-agouti`: 142 editable blocks; 25 protected directive/shebang lines; final description 6,963 chars.\n- `doddered-undercover-alligator`: 130 editable blocks; 25 protected directive/shebang lines; final description 6,999 chars.\n- `fishy-dinky-urus`: 99 editable blocks; 7 protected directive/shebang lines; final description 5,592 chars.\n- `dripping-captious-arctichare`: 198 editable blocks; 39 protected directive/shebang lines; final description 7,849 chars.\nAll descriptions are below the 8,000-character review admission cap. Stable IDs are unique and span-qualified; owner/spans and file-impact order were validated; every impact path has a reason.\n\nCorrections and protected consumers:\n- Replaced the former stale prose-audit basis with the immutable SHA above and audited current bytes.\n- Kept FastAPI `health`, `webhook`, and `rerun` docstrings out of editable scope because OpenAPI consumes them.\n- Kept the `mcp_server.py` module docstring protected because facade tests inspect it.\n- Kept the `mirror_guard.py` module docstring protected because argparse publishes it.\n- Preserved every `yaml-language-server` directive byte-for-byte.\n- Limited the editable `src/rebar/config.py` comment through line 202; line 203 is a protected directive.\n- Removed `runtime.py:44-47` from editable scope because it includes a directive and contains only 37 words of non-directive current rationale; this corrected the reconciler total from 199 to 198 blocks.\n- Corrected the workflow focused contract to `tests/unit/test_criterion_preview.py` and made it verify the editor build leaves `dist/` unchanged.\n\nVerification design:\n- Each ticket now has the same six DD records: `immutable-prose-only`, `exact-leaf-paths`, `comment-hygiene`, `focused-contracts`, `diff-integrity`, and `repository-gates`.\n- The immutable oracle parses Python with `type_comments=True`, normalizes only allowlisted owner docstrings plus `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`, compares the remaining AST/runtime tree, preserves directive/shebang physical lines, rejects zero-context hunks outside immutable-base spans, permits only comment/blank additions for JS/JSX, and requires ordered YAML non-comment/nonblank lines to remain byte-identical.\n- All four immutable-oracle commands executed successfully; all 24 stored commands passed `zsh -n`. A repository-wide search at the pinned SHA for `__doc__` / `inspect.getdoc` consumers confirmed the exclusions above.\n\nWrite/readback receipt:\n- Wrote each description, exact file-impact array, and six-command DD array through the rebar MCP server, serially by ticket.\n- Every value was then read back independently through MCP: all four descriptions match byte-for-byte; all ordered file-impact and verify-command arrays match field-for-field; all four tickets remain open, unassigned, and under the expected parent.\n- One final DD write was committed locally but initially reported `push_status=pending` because the tracker write lock stayed busy during non-fast-forward recovery. The exact payload was present on readback. Repeating the identical MCP setter once (it is declared idempotent) exercised the documented next-write recovery and returned `push_status=ok` with no warnings.\n- Only normal MCP ticket-event auto-commit/auto-push behavior occurred. No manual ticket-branch git operation or manual push was used. No code files, claims, plan reviews, transitions, commits, or repository gates were performed."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788627830916143673,"uuid":"db6f5a96-2e83-47c2-a385-d8e1d39d0d4f"}